<title>ESTONIA: SOCCER - ESTONIA 1, LATVIA 3 - RESULT.</title>
<headline>SOCCER - ESTONIA 1, LATVIA 3 - RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-05-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Latvia beat Estonia 3-1</p>
<p>(halftime 0-1) in their World Cup European group four</p>
<p>qualifying match on Sunday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Estonia - Indrek Zelinski 5</p>
<p>Latvia - Vladimir Babitches 53, Aleksandr Jeliseev 78,</p>
<p>Marek Lemsalu own goal 86</p>
<p>Teams:  Estonia - 1-Mart Poom, 2-Marek Lemsalu, 3-Urmas</p>
<p>Kirs, 4-Raivo Nommik, 5-Janek Meet, 6-Viktor Alonen, 7-Kristen</p>
<p>Vikmae (14-Argo Arbeiter, 81), 8-Indrek Zelinski, 9-Marko</p>
<p>Kristal, 10-Martin Reim, 11-Andres Oper (18-Meelis Rooba, 83)</p>
<p>Latvia - 1-Oleg Koravaev, 2-Igor Stepanov (16-Aleksandr</p>
<p>Jeliseev, 78), 3-Vitali Astafiev, 4-Mikhail Zesulinski, 5-Jouri</p>
<p>Chevliakov, 6-Imant Bleidelis, 7-Valeri Ivanov, 8-Marian</p>
<p>Pakhar, 9-Vitas Rimkus (17-Roland Bulder, 74), 10-Vladimir</p>
<p>Babitches, 11-Andrej Stolcer.</p>
<p>Red card: Estonia - Viktor Alonen 61.</p>
<p>    Standings	 P   W   D   L   F   A  Pts </p>
<p>Scotland		7   4   2   1   8   2   14</p>
<p>Austria		 5   3   1   1   5   3   10</p>
<p>Sweden		  5   3   0   2   9   5    9</p>
<p>Latvia		  6   2   1   3   8   8    7</p>
<p>Belarus		 5   1   1   3   3   9    4</p>
<p>Estonia		 6   1   1   4   2   8    4</p>
<p>Next matches: June 8 - Latvia v Austria, Estonia v Sweden,</p>
<p>Belarus v Scotland</p>
<p>    -- Tallinn newsroom, +372 638 400</p>
